sometimes I'm asked about how to resolve  relationship conflict and I find this  amusing and I'm smiling because this has  never been a strong suit for me as it  relates to intimate relationships I am  NOT famous for my patience and have  caused innumerable problems in my  relationships as a result of that and  grew up at least through schooling and  coaching with very little positive  reinforcement a lot of negative  reinforcement which also doesn't help  matters but I have found a few different  approaches and frameworks perhaps tools  also that have helped me greatly  personally to be a better partner to my  girlfriend for instance and also tools  that help us together as a couple to  resolve conflict it's not about avoiding  conflict I think that there's a certain  amount of conflict that can be avoided  but whenever you are spending 24/7  together or in close proximity you're  going to have friction in the system and  that is certainly true with even my  closest maybe especially my closest guy  friends but let's talk about the tools  first I believe that to minimize  conflict or quickly resolve conflict you  need to first become more aware of your  internal States and become more aware of  the stories that you create in your head  the loops that you play that will inform  how you interact with someone else  because if for instance you create a  story where you were always the victim  and that is your pattern that will  greatly affect how you approach any type  of conflict resolution or discussion and  two tools I found very very helpful for  that on number one sam harris is waking  up up i highly recommend getting it i  have no skin in the game no equity no  payoff and hook kickbacks nothing so sam  harris is waking up app which provides a  logical progression of skill development  in meditation or really self-awareness  that's number one it gives you a 10  minute practice each day that i do in  the mornings i still use this app i've  run  multiple times it's exceptional that  pairs very well with a book called  awareness and for some reason it has  multiple subtitles depending on the  format one of them is I believe the  promises and perils of reality the other  is conversations with the masters but  that doesn't make any sense because  there's really only one author and that  is Anthony de Mello so the book title is  awareness the author Anthony de Mello de  mal o who was a Jesuit priest and also a  psychotherapist very interesting  combination and that book will also help  you to recognize the stories the movies  you're creating as an interpretation of  events it will also help you to become  very bluntly honest with yourself in a  self-assessment so that you are able to  spot where you genuinely want to fix  problems or where you are more wedded to  drama perhaps and those two tools  combined especially have been incredibly  valuable for me and that's kind of step  one my girlfriend has also gone through  both of these and it's helped us to  pause because between the stimulus and  your response there is a gap and in the  gap is where everything can change  that's where you get to choose your  response to be a response able okay  so step number one is really working on  yourself to be a better partner then as  a couple I think having a very candid  assessment of your sensitivities and pet  peeves is very important for instance my  girlfriend at some point this was maybe  six months ago nine months ago asked me  about wordsmithing she wanted to know  how she could craft feedback in the  perfect way she didn't phrase it that  way but in a better way such that I  would be more receptive to certain types  of feedback and we were doing a  quarterly couples work which I also  recommend so having sometimes  facilitator like a therapist at least  once a quarter to a  assist with a couples day that we block  out we do this once a quarter and during  one of those sessions I said it's not  about the content it's about the timing  and I think this is true for a lot of  couples rather than having things  piecemeal throughout the day it is  helpful for some of us especially  someone like me who is wedded to  structure and predictability as much as  possible you might not think that might  not expect that but it's true on a daily  basis I thrive with structure and I said  it doesn't matter what the word smithing  is you could be you could be Tolstoy you  could be Nabokov it doesn't matter I I  need things to be timed in a particular  way that would be my preference and so  we set aside on a say weekly or  bi-weekly basis a batching session and  the batching session allows us to  discuss what it is that we need what it  is that's bothering us and the framework  or I should say the format we've used  and I'm not aware of any reading we've  done that has informed this way it was  trial and error is we first talk about  what the other person is doing well what  we love what we'd love more of right now  what we love more of is gonna come again  but what the other person what our  partners doing well then we talk about  what we think we're doing well  personally and then we talk about what  we would like even more of okay rather  than saying what you're [ __ ] up what  you're screwing up what's driving me  crazy it's like you know what I would  really enjoy more of what would really  make me happy to get more of his ex and  that type of very simple format has  worked for us and it is recorded not  necessarily audio recorded but the the  takeaways the homework assignments are  recorded if you do something like  Evernote you could use notes so that  there's follow-up without follow-up this  is all pissin in the wind so you need  follow-up so there are then the meeting  notes so to speak from this batching  session and we each get a copy and this  way we can do two things we can refer  back to it so that for the neck  at least several days following that  back just batching session refer to that  say in the mornings as a reminder and  then when we do our next batching  session we can see how we've done we can  look at the at the assignment and then  the report card and sometimes I'll fall  short and I'll beg God you know I  supposed to do that I totally blind him  so sorry there's an accountability that  is really important all right so we've  talked about a couple things so far we  talked about waking up at Sam Harris we  talked about awareness Anthony de Mello  we've talked about batching sessions and  I also mentioned in passing these  quarterly couples and days it's an  entire day set aside let's just call it  from like 10 a.m. to 8 p.m. something  like that to talk and to have some type  of facilitation and it can be very  freeform in this case there's less  structure and it's really just talking  about whatever's on our mind  whatever our wants our are our needs  being met our things bothering us are  our desires payment whatever it might be  and for me at least these tools and  having this type of structure has been  invaluable and last but not least as my  friend of all raava Khan  one of the best investors and  entrepreneurs I know has said and I'm  gonna paraphrase if you want to avoid  conflict step number one is do not  associate with people who are always in  conflict right so choose your friends  choose your partners very wisely you  were gonna be the average of the five  people you associate with most so choose  wisely  good luck  you
 

